# Docs Sync

`README.md` is the source of truth for this project. Any code change that affects the items below must include a corresponding documentation update **in the same commit**.

| You changed… | Update… |
|---|---|
| HTTP routes or response codes | `README.md` (API section) |
| Environment variables | `README.md` + `.env.example` |
| GIF generation behavior (VHS settings, output format, tape structure) | `README.md` |
| Package responsibilities or exported interfaces | inline godoc comments |
| A known anti-pattern is fixed or a new one is discovered | `TODO.md` |
| A 3rd-party tool or SDK changes (VHS, New Relic, Gin) | `README.md` (dependencies section) |

## Definition of Done checklist

Before declaring a task complete, verify:

- [ ] All affected sections of `README.md` updated
- [ ] `.env.example` has a key for every new env var (no value)
- [ ] No new route was added without an entry in the README API table
- [ ] Every required env var causes `log.Fatal` at startup if missing
- [ ] Fan-out goroutines use `sync.WaitGroup`, not `errgroup`, for independent operations
